 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Amazon EventBridge API (2015-10-07). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Custom event buses, their event-pattern rules, archives and connections are stored as configuration metadata: no event is accepted, matched, archived, replayed or delivered, and PutEvents, PutTargets, StartReplay and the other delivery APIs return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. The account's default event bus and partner event buses are not modeled: rule operations require EventBusName to name a custom event bus, schedule expressions (which AWS supports only on the default bus) are refused, and every rule needs a JSON event pattern whose values are arrays or objects. PutRule on an existing rule replaces only the members it supplies; omitted members keep their stored values instead of being cleared. Connections support BASIC and API_KEY authorization and are reported AUTHORIZED without contacting any endpoint; OAuth client credentials, private connectivity and secret invocation parameters are refused. Passwords and API key values stay in the private simulator database, are never returned, and no Secrets Manager secret is created. UpdateConnection replaces AuthParameters as a whole, so it requires AuthorizationType and complete credentials. Event buses with rules cannot be deleted; archives keep their EventSourceArn when the bus is deleted. Only rules and event buses can be tagged. The Limit member of list operations without an official paginator and NamePrefix filters are refused.",
  "title": "Amazon EventBridge (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2015-10-07"
 },
